# Component & UI Standards

## 1. Hierarchy
- **UI primitive:** shared low-level components (Button, Input, Card, Table,
  Dialog…) live in `@/components/ui`. This is a local shadcn-style kit on top of
  `radix-ui` + `@base-ui/react`.
- **Feature component:** business-logic UI lives in `@/features/[name]/components`.
- **Composition:** route pages compose feature components; feature components
  compose UI primitives.

## 2. Do Not Reinvent Primitives
- Before building any interactive element, check `src/components/ui/` — it
  already includes table, card, chart, sidebar, dialog, sheet, drawer,
  dropdown-menu, popover, calendar, combobox, command, pagination, tabs,
  tooltip, skeleton, empty, badge, progress, and more.
- Missing one? Add it with the `shadcn` MCP / CLI. Don't hand-roll it and don't
  edit an existing primitive's internals to fit a single feature — wrap it.

## 3. Accessibility (a11y)
- Prefer the provided Radix/Base-UI primitives for menus, dialogs, tabs, tooltips —
  they carry keyboard + screen-reader support.
- Icons: `lucide-react` only. Use the `size` prop, not arbitrary `w-/h-` classes.
- Every icon-only button gets an accessible label (translation key).
- Tables use `<caption>`/`scope` via the `table` primitive; don't fake tables with divs.

## 4. Dashboard Building Blocks
- **StatCard** — one per feature, built on `Card`.
- **Charts** — always through `@/components/ui/chart` (`ChartContainer` +
  typed `ChartConfig`); colors from theme CSS variables. Never import `recharts`
  into a route file.
- **Data tables** — `@/components/ui/table` + `@/components/ui/pagination`; table
  state in a hook.
- **Loading** — a pixel-perfect skeleton mirroring the real markup, reused for
  `isLoading` and `<Suspense>`. No spinners for content, no layout shift.
  Full workflow in the `create-loading-skeletons` skill.
- **Empty** — `@/components/ui/empty` with a message and optional CTA.

## 5. Container / Presentational Balance
- Components render UI; data logic lives in the feature's custom hook.
- A component over **200 lines** must be split into sub-components in the same
  feature folder.

## 6. Styling & Theming
- All styling rules live in @styling.md — Tailwind v4, semantic tokens, **no
  arbitrary values / hex** (`bg-[#F5F5F5]` → `bg-muted`; `p-[15px]` → `p-4`).
- Pass `className` only for spacing/layout; use a primitive's `variant`/`size`
  props for everything else.
- **Dark mode** (theme provider, e.g. `next-themes` — it works in Vite): every
  new surface must work in light and dark — automatic when you use tokens.
  Chart colors come from `--chart-*` via `ChartConfig`, so they theme for free.
